# PM GitHub Workflow .gitignore

# SECRETS
# Scoped to real credential FILES (not bare substrings), so a doc named
# token-economy-prd.md or secret-sauce-strategy.md is NOT swallowed.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
api-keys.md
secrets/
secrets.*
credentials.json
*-credentials.json
*credential*.json
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*-adminsdk*.json
*token*.json
*token*.txt
*secret*.json
*secret*.yaml
*secret*.yml
id_rsa
id_rsa.pub
id_ed25519
.npmrc
.pypirc
# Cloud / infra credentials (the most-leaked files in real repos)
.aws/
.aws*
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.kube/config
.docker/config.json
gha-creds-*.json
application_default_credentials.json
# A scanner is the real safety net — this repo ships .github/workflows/gitleaks.yml.

# OS FILES
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# NODE / NPM
node_modules/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
bun.lockb

# PYTHON
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# LARGE DATA FILES
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/raw/
exports/
recordings/
transcripts/raw/
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.wav
*.m4a
*.mov
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# CLAUDE CODE
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/statsig/
# Activated skill copies. The source of truth is skills/; .claude/skills/ is a
# local convenience copy (see README), so it shouldn't be committed twice.
.claude/skills/

# IDE FILES
.vscode/
.cursor/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# BUILD ARTIFACTS
dist/
build/
out/
*.log
.next/
.vercel/

# PM-SPECIFIC
*.otter
*.granola
drafts/wip/
scratch/
screenshots/
screen-recordings/

# RESEARCH OUTPUTS (often contain customer PII / verbatim quotes)
# Anchored to the DATED filenames the skills emit (feedback-synthesis-2026-...,
# competitor-acme-2026-...) and to research directories — so a template or doc
# like interview-prep.md or competitor-analysis-framework.md is NOT swallowed,
# but a real dated output is. Want to share a sanitized one? `git add -f <file>`
feedback-synthesis-2[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.md
competitor-*-2[0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.md
interviews/
transcripts/
*-raw.*
data/exports/
# Re-include the repo's shipped source, so a dated PII output dropped into
# skills/ or evals/ still gets caught while the source files stay committable.
!skills/*/SKILL.md
!evals/*-criteria.md
!evals/how-to-write-eval-criteria.md

# ENTERPRISE NOTE
# Add regulated document types here
# Consider CODEOWNERS for review requirements
# NDA materials should NEVER be in any repo
